    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d930">

                <pb facs="0866" n="762" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg762"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/6611.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Ciudad
                            Juarez to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso, Texas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-03-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 10, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Reports from the south and west do not show conditions improving. Every
                    indication justifies the claim of the anti-Government faction and they are daily
                    growing in number. It is also becoming apparent that the struggle now augmenting
                    will prove to be a real war.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwards</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
